# Which issue(s) this PR fixes:

This should close #18.

# What this PR does / why we need it:

ThinBridge BHO does not redirect a URL loading in a subframe to the default browser (defined at the `[Default]` section), if it is not match to any matching rule for specific browsers, despite configured to redirect loading in subframes.

# How to verify the fixed issue:

Try loading of a webpage containing one or more subframes which is not matched to any rule.

## The steps to verify:

1. Install ThinBridge.
2. Install Google Chrome.
3. Activate Internet Explorer.
4. Put `ThinBridgeBHO.ini` with following contents:
   ```
   [GLOBAL]
   @DISABLED
   @REDIRECT_PAGE_ACTION:1
   @INTRANET_ZONE
   @TRUSTED_ZONE
   @RDP_APPMODE
   
   [Default]
   @BROWSER_PATH:Chrome
   @REDIRECT_PAGE_ACTION:0
   @CLOSE_TIMEOUT:3
   
   [CUSTOM18]
   @BROWSER_PATH:
   @REDIRECT_PAGE_ACTION:0
   @CLOSE_TIMEOUT:3
   *.microsoft.com*
   ```
5. Run `cmd.exe`.
6. Run `"C:\Program Files (x86)\Internet Explorer\iexplore.exe" https://powerbi.microsoft.com/ja-jp/`.

## Expected result:

A loading with the URL `https://publisher.liveperson.net/` in a subframe is canceled and redirected to Google Chrome.
